{"answer": "It is denied by default. `authorityOf` in `apps/api/src/oversight/toolAuthority.ts` treats a tool with no row as `requires_human_action`, so it never executes. This holds at both enforcement points. `authorityOf` only matches the table's own keys, so an inherited name like `toString` is denied too.

The oversight gate (`withHumanOversight`) never calls the executor of a `requires_human_action` tool. It returns a constant result, `{"error":"requires_human_action","escalation":"blocked_consequential_call"}`, as a normal `ToolResponse` and does not throw.

The api also refuses to start if the live tool registry contains a name the table doesn't cover. This is the `assertAllToolsDeclared.ts` check (FR-004).", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-human-oversight/spec.md (FR-003, FR-004)", "pull-280", "issue-33", "issue-445", "issue-448", "docs/human-oversight.md"]}

